# Backend Review

## Checklist

- Routes use nouns (plural), correct HTTP methods, and correct status codes.
- All authenticated endpoints actually check auth — no missing middleware.
- Authorization checks ownership (IDOR risk): user A cannot access user B's data.
- Input validated and sanitised at the boundary.
- No PII or tokens in responses or logs.
- Rate limiting on auth and high-cost endpoints.
- No string-interpolated SQL — parameterised queries only.
- No N+1 queries. Paginated list endpoints.
- Errors handled with consistent response shape.
- External calls have timeouts. Multi-write operations use transactions.
- New endpoints have integration tests (success, auth fail, bad input, not found).

## Output Format

